# Sibling git worktrees checked out under the repo — their files belong to other branches, and the
# anchored patterns below (fixtures/**, spec/...) don't match under this prefix, so a root
# `pnpm format` would reformat another branch's byte-exact goldens.
.claude/

# Keep the user's plan and the vendored upstream prose spec verbatim
PLAN.md
spec/ai-catalog.md

# Vendored verbatim from ards-project/ard-spec (see spec/ard/README.md) — never reformat
spec/ard/spec/
spec/ard/conformance/

# Next.js generated files
**/next-env.d.ts

# Machine-generated report-snapshot goldens (written by scripts/verify-report-snapshots.mjs via
# JSON.stringify on each `reports:regen`) — reformatting them would drift from what that script
# writes and break the next regen's diff.
fixtures/**/report.golden.json

# Twin snapshots are byte-exact copies of what ax generates (normalized timestamps only) — a
# reformat would diverge them from the generated output the snapshot script diffs against.
fixtures/**/twins.golden/
